EASD: Driving in Spikes: An Entropy-Guided Object Detector for Spike Cameras
Research: Ziyan Liu, Qi Su, Lulu Tang, Zhaofei Yu, and Tiejun Huang.

YOLO framework and decoder
  Source: https://github.com/bubbliiiing/yolov5-pytorch
  Original repository license: GNU GPL version 3; retained in LICENSE.
  Adapted components include CSPDarknet, YOLO loss, decoding, target assignment,
  EMA utilities, and evaluation helpers. EASD modifications include spike-native
  temporal/spatial branches, input/coordinate handling, training entry points,
  entropy routing fixes, and release documentation.

CAMixerSR
  Source: https://github.com/icandle/CAMixerSR
  Copyright 2024 CAMixerSR Authors
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  The full license is preserved in LICENSES/CAMixerSR-Apache-2.0.txt.
  Modified components in nets/spatial.py include window attention, offset
  warping, predictor, layer normalization, and gated feed-forward blocks.
  EASD replaces learned mask routing with entropy-based routing and uses
  per-sample foreground selection. Checkpoint parameter names are retained.

Figures and data
  Paper figures and author-provided visualizations are identified in
  docs/ASSETS.md. Dataset rights and access terms remain with their respective
  providers. The repository does not include the full datasets or checkpoints.
